## Build prerequisites

Read-only package preflight found Amazon Linux packages Rust/Cargo 1.97.0. SSM command `72330950-d60e-4ddf-b89a-854f3d11c6ca` installed signed Amazon Linux `cargo`, `rust`, and `gcc` packages plus dependencies. Verified:

- `cargo 1.97.0 (Amazon Linux 1.97.0-2.amzn2023)`
- `rustc 1.97.0 (Amazon Linux 1.97.0-2.amzn2023)`
- 27 GiB remained free

No service changed. The t3.small will not compile the Rust/ONNX release.

Two off-host AL2023 link attempts established an ABI incompatibility rather than a missing compiler package. `ort-sys` rc13's prebuilt static archive references glibc ≥2.38 `__isoc23_strtol`, `__isoc23_strtoll`, `__isoc23_strtoull` and a newer libstdc++ `std::__cxx11::basic_string::_M_replace_cold`; AL2023 supplies glibc 2.34 and GCC/libstdc++ 11. Installing the correct `gcc-c++` package did not resolve it. Cached-Titan read-only runtime does not load MiniLM, but the immutable app links ONNX Runtime unconditionally.

The reviewed pivot is a pinned Ubuntu 24.04 runtime container, not an app feature change. Compatibility-only source `3970a769ca5152bd5ddfd8ec1402e26b1d06eef5` built off-host from an isolated exact worktree with the committed lockfile. Do not deploy this revision: a later app fix removes stale-telemetry Similar leakage, and its snapshot may retain those vectors. Binary SHA-256: `47bbff8ef64657b75a171d4fc2e116a96e643a0b578450877ecb8c66c3e772d9`. The runtime base is `ubuntu:24.04@sha256:a61567bd31828687156d735ea8eb01ba4e37636e225dd6a48ba94136a70d9d61`; local image ID `sha256:6dc413104651e7e3a6e29093197a66dd69823a344b26fe1964dd275787ae3bf3`, 48,181,324 bytes, numeric non-root user 10001.

A consistent 225,124,352-byte SDK snapshot passed integrity and contains 9,016 raw signed events, 174,216 social edges, planner statistics, MiniLM vectors, 119 cached Titan post vectors and six Titan topics assigning all119. Snapshot SHA-256: `efe16d6e03fd0c14e01a21251748eb2883384281307b14855f577a1d5c6fc322`.

The first read-only container start exposed a packaging failure: SQLite WAL mode requires a writable directory even when the main database file and application are read-only. Keeping `events.sqlite` bind-mounted read-only while mounting a 16 MiB `/data` tmpfs for WAL/SHM fixed it. Compatibility smoke returned root HTTP200/100 cards in 0.30 s, status200/0.11 s, cached Titan topic200/37 cards in 0.29 s, cached Titan Similar200/100 cards in 0.44 s, and uncached Titan Meaning400 without AWS. A private Caddy canary on an existing-network equivalent resolved `meatybroth-rust:8088` and returned root/status/Titan topic200 in 0.12–0.32 s. Caddy needs only `NET_BIND_SERVICE`; dropping that file capability prevents its executable from starting.

Transfer archive `/tmp/meatybroth-deploy-3970a76.tar` is 130,191,360 bytes with SHA-256 `f2470fd1c3fef51efefd1762d43a883124b1acb2c162a8cf4710bd2023a632d4`. No transfer occurred because AWS login refresh remains unavailable.

