Revision `5dca648a2676ea261905a06c9f35a23d2dc58d2d` added one-failure protection. Its runtime package also added CA bundle SHA-256 `ecd9dc38bc3efb7dbd6431f57e29d2f8d6a0f0d211e1464b3fef2cbfe266fcd2`. Release binary SHA-256 was `8247cfa69d8d303c6f751d43a3a717b371f30f6127845d124545d9822bd3f7f5`; the EC2 image config ID is `sha256:0e6ca3a16664583a2427f527a08b524079a7f62b71e718045f9c4617b2b35865`.

The intended one-request diagnostic isolation failed because `MEATYBROTH_EMBED_DEADLINE_EPOCH=0` does not gate `embed_recent_pending`. One successful cached-query preflight enabled ordinary concurrency. Before stop, 279 requests succeeded with 627,264 tokens and $0.01254528 actual cost; 85 newly admitted posts embedded with p50 7 seconds, maximum 42 seconds and zero over 300 seconds. The 30-second stop ended with SIGKILL and added eight uncertain and two reserved rows. These states remain in the canonical database. This was a deployment-control error, not an unauthorized budget increase; continuous collection was already authorized.

The sole continuous writer started at 22:14:47Z. A cached Meaning request completed HTTP 200 in 11 seconds. Private Status, Topics, cached Meaning and Similar all returned HTTP 200 before the route switch. Caddy first remained on the old upstream because `sed -i` replaced the host file inode while the container retained the old bind-mounted inode. Restarting only Caddy remounted the validated file; active upstream then became `meatybroth-rust-next:8088` at about 22:22:56Z. The writer was not interrupted.

