## Host recovery and responsive reader, 2026-09-14

A bounded `strace` attempt did not terminate through `timeout` after SSM cancellation. SSM stopped heartbeating and public Status also stopped responding. A soft reboot did not recover the OS management path, so the instance was force-stopped at 22:47:59Z and returned SSM-online after start at 22:50:52Z. The EBS database recovered with `integrity_check=ok`. The reboot-cleared `/tmp` contained zero matching trace files at inspection; no raw syscall trace was copied or published. The recovered ledger initially contained 13,608 succeeded, 73 uncertain and three reserved Bedrock rows.

Revision `5dca648` auto-started. To upgrade without abandoning a provider request, the container was briefly paused and the live ledger sampled until it contained exactly the three historical reserved Bedrock rows. This clean paid boundary occurred at epoch `1789340198` on attempt 20. The paused process was killed; the post-stop ledger still contained exactly three reserved rows.

