`strace` caused the host incident and did not produce usable bottleneck evidence. The targeted application measurements distinguish the reader work: zero-card Topics 0.79 seconds, while the 100-card New response spent 4.21 seconds server-side and emitted 6.57 MB. This supports bounded-card-query and response-size work, not a claim that WAL size or RSS alone caused the stall.

